# The modules and wrappers of `pg` that `access` may call (design item 14), by path, each with its reason; a line
# naming a module lets in every function under it. The typed lint refuses any other path from `access` into `pg`.

pg::PgError	the error an `access` function returns, with Postgres' SQLSTATE and message, which the entry raises
pg::word	a datum's word read as a value passed by value and made from one, which is arithmetic on the word
pg::Att	an attribute of a slot's descriptor as `slot_att` packs it: its type, length, and flags
pg::slot_natts	a slot's descriptor: how many attributes it has
pg::slot_att	a slot's descriptor: one attribute's packed word
pg::slot_store	a slot: a stored row's key columns, key, tuple, and value ids copied into the slot's own buffer
pg::slot_keyed	a slot: the stored row's key columns, lent while the slot is
pg::slot_key	a slot: the stored row's key, lent while the slot is
pg::slot_tuple	a slot: the stored row's tuple, lent while the slot is
pg::slot_filled	a slot: how many attributes of the stored row are deformed
pg::slot_set_null	a slot: the next attribute's value set to NULL
pg::slot_set_word	a slot: the next attribute's value set to a word passed by value
pg::slot_set_fixed	a slot: the next attribute's value copied into the slot's buffer at its type's alignment
pg::slot_set_varlena	a slot: the next attribute's value written into the slot's buffer under a varlena header
pg::slot_system	a slot: a system attribute, which Postgres' virtual slot answers or refuses
pg::slot_copy_values	a slot: another slot's values copied into it, as Postgres' virtual slot copies them
pg::CatalogCaps	the capabilities a key's encoder hands `sort_key`
pg::sort_key	a text's sort key under its collation, Postgres' `pg_strnxfrm`
pg::sort_key_of	a text's sort key under its collation into a buffer of its own size, `pg_strnxfrm` asked again when the first was too short
pg::slot_set_missing	a slot: the next attribute's value set to its descriptor's missing value
pg::slot_writer	a slot: the stored row's version, its writer
pg::slot_command	a slot: the stored row's version, its writer's command
pg::slot_deleter	a slot: the stored row's version, its deleter
pg::slot_deleter_command	a slot: the stored row's version, its deleter's command
pg::ffi::DgStored	a stored row's version, table, values' TOAST relation, ctid, and deform's room as the slot's store takes them: nine integers passed by value
pg::slot_att_storage	a slot: an attribute's storage kind, its descriptor's attstorage
pg::slot_table	a slot: the stored row's table's object id
pg::slot_tid	a slot: the stored row's ctid
pg::slot_values	a slot: the stored row's value ids of its values out of line, lent while the slot is
pg::slot_toast	a slot: the stored row's values' TOAST relation's object id
pg::slot_set_external	a slot: the next attribute's value set to Postgres' on-disk TOAST pointer of a value out of line
pg::slot_transform	a slot: the stored row's transform to its reader's epoch, lent while the slot is
